speechtext:
How much money, if any, was spent as a result of the royal commission on coasting trade for
(a)	remuneration to the individual commissioners;
(b)	the staff of the royal commission; <c) travelling expenses of the commission, the staff; (d) other expenses not mentioned above?
Answer by: Hon. George H. Hees (Minister of Transport):
Up to March 31, 1958, only (a) $48,367.00; (b) $78,226.03; (c) $19,006.33 and $13,591.83;
(d)	other expenses such as professional services; advertising; printing and office supplies; telephone and telegrams, $92,403.49.
